[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1294","stub":{"id":"1294","section":"Powley Place to Stratford","altname":"","river":"East Canada Creek","difficulty":"IItoIV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"895","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112080","location":{"latitude":"43.3092002868652","longitude":"-74.6540985107422"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117357","location":{"latitude":"43.1800994873047","longitude":"-74.6948013305664"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"12","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"1294","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"5000cfs or a jump of 2000 cfs in a day are needed for this to be runnable.\n\nFrom David Brucas\n\n“The start of this section is on a seasonal road. If the snow is cleared, you may still be blocked by a government gate located at 43.27429, -74.66443 (about 1.7 miles past the last bridge). Park there and bushwack to the creek, walk up river a quarter mile to catch a major rapid. (As of April 2010 there was a river wide strainer in between the drops of this rapid. HUGE tree trunk, needs a\n\nchainsaw team.) Map from last bridge to the gate is http://goo.gl/maps/3Jfd\n\nIf the road is not cleared of snow, you can put in at the bridge that crosses this river at the end of the full season Piseco Road, (43.25483, -74.65369) \\[The seasonal road starts exactly at the bridge. As with many adk seasonal roads, if it's covered with snow, you will most likely get stuck if you drive in. Every dip gets deep snow, snow hides the road edges making it very easy to drop your wheels into the ditches either side, snow hide big potholes. I've seen cars and vans stuck up there multiple times and left there until the spring thaw. Don't be\n\nfoolish.\\]”\n\nFrom Tim Trezise\n\n“From Oregon Bridge to take out at \"broken dam\": a bunch of class III fun interspersed with 3 significant IV drops starting with\n\n1) \"Cable Car\" (a double drop), then\n\n2) Triple Drop (a slide funneling into a 4' drop into a keeper hole (boof left) then just downstream a big boof over an 8' falls, then after some great class III slides and ledges to\n\n3) Broken Dam (run the left side boof)\n\nthen take out, climb back up over the drop (river left) and walk up the trail to the secondary road.\n\nCheck out the pics and video clips to get an idea. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tb2OktdQK-M\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1AOGUkXofek\n\nCheck  Dennis Squires book New York Exposed (volume 2) for a description of this section.\n\n**Mohawk Valley Area Reaches**\n\n[Canajoharie Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10885/) [Caroga Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1272/) [Cincinnati Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3568/)\n\n[East Canada Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1294/) [Fish Creek, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1306/) [Ninemile Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1361/)\n\n[North Chuctanunda Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10884/) [Nowadaga Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5034/) [Mohawk (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1348/)\n\n[Oriskany Creek (Clinton)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10867/)[Oriskany Creek (Oriskany Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10630/) [Schoharie Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1419/)\n\n[Sprite Creek (Upper)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1425/) [Sprite Creek (Lower)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5062/) [Spruce Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1426/)\n\n[Timmerman Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/408/) [West Canada Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1453/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)**","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"12.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"1294","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"5000","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"15000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SACANDAGA RIVER NEAR HOPE NY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01321000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"895","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.86","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"43.3534722","longitude":"-74.2684722"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01321000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01321000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nToo Low to Boat (L0-L9): 0 - 5000 cfs  Comment: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 5000 - 15000 cfs  Comment: Upper limit estimated.  The river will also be running if the gauge has jumped 2000cfs in a day.\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but does